{"type":"message","id":"1dc545b2","parentId":"1d7956ed","timestamp":"2026-03-14T06:20:37.416Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to:\n\n1. Set up cron jobs that run hourly at specific times:\n   - 01:10 (1st hour of each day) → fetch channel\n   - 01:25 (15 minutes after first) → second check  \n   - 01:40 (heartbeat, 15 minutes after last)\n\nWait, let me re-read this. They want ALL of these to run hourly, just shifted by offsets:\n- First job at minute :10 each hour\n- Second job at minute :25 each hour (15 min offset from first)\n- Heartbeat job at minute :40 each hour (another 15 min offset)\n\nSo the schedule is:\n- Every hour on the :10 → fetch channel task\n- Every hour on the :25 → second check  \n- Every hour on the :40 → heartbeat\n\nI'll use cron \"at\" schedules with ISO timestamps that repeat each hour. For a 24-hour day, I need to specify all hours (or use a repeating pattern). Let me construct these properly:\n\nFor \"hourly at :10\":\n```json\n{\n  \"schedule\": {\n    \"kind\": \"at\",\n    \"at\": \"2026-03-14T01:10:00Z\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nBut this is a one-time job. I need hourly repeating. Let me think... The cron system uses either:\n- `everyMs` for intervals (not quite what we want - that's fixed intervals, not hour-specific times)\n- `cron` expressions with timezone\n- Multiple `at` jobs to cover all hours\n\nActually, looking at the schema again, `everyMs` might work if we anchor it properly. But we want specific minutes (:10, :25, :40), not every N milliseconds from some origin.\n\n\nI'll need to create multiple one-shot jobs across each hour of the day to capture the precise timing requirements. This means generating entries for 24 hours × 3 jobs = 72 total cron entries to ensure comprehensive coverage.\n\nFor the fetch channel task, I'll use a systemEvent payload that retrieves Telegram data and summarizes it into MEMORY.md with relevant context. The heartbeat check will verify LM Studio connectivity on port 3003 and pull recent logs for any errors. Each job needs careful configuration: setting sessionTarget to \"isolated\" with an agentTurn payload that includes the appropriate task description, model reference, and timeout settings tailored to each operation's complexity.\n\nThe GitHub Pages sites in `D:\\AI_PROJECTS\\projects` will auto-deploy when pushed, but I need to confirm which repositories actually require this deployment behavior before finalizing their configurations."},{"type":"text","text":"I'll set up the hourly cron jobs for your tasks as specified:\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"403070820","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"D:\\AI_PROJECTS\\projects"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen3-5-9b","model":"qwen3.5-9b-claude-4.6-opus-reasoning-distilled","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773468957421}}
