{"type":"message","id":"c945b906","parentId":"7e5ac4a5","timestamp":"2026-03-14T06:31:15.820Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The three hourly cron jobs have been successfully created! Let me verify they're all set up correctly and explain what's happening. The anchor time I used (1741958200000) corresponds to March 13, 2026 at 1:00 AM Riyadh time, which means the hourly jobs will run at exactly :10, :25, and :40 as specified.\n\nNow I need to address the user's second request about making the mimic dashboard a daily brief they can read for 5 minutes. This likely means adding a feature or setting that allows them to view the dashboard content for 5 minutes before it expires or refreshes.\n\nHowever, looking at their tools and capabilities, this is probably referring to a web browser session or a local application that displays the mimic dashboard. Since I don't have direct control over their browser sessions or applications outside of OpenClaw's workspace, I'll need to clarify what they want me to do about the 5-minute viewing feature.\n\nLet me respond with the cron job status and ask for clarification on the dashboard requirement."},{"type":"text","text":"I've successfully set up **three hourly cron jobs** that run in this order:\n\n## ⏰ Scheduled Jobs Created\n\n| Job Name | Schedule | Action |\n|----------|----------|--------|\n| **Daily Brief Fetch - @:10** | Every hour at :10 | Fetch Telegram channel & process briefs |\n| **Process Briefs - @:25** | Every hour at :25 | Analyze daily brief content |\n| **Heartbeat Health Check - @:40** | Every hour at :40 | System health monitoring |\n\n### Timeline Visualization\n```\nHour 1:    1:10 → Fetch   │  1:25 → Process │  1:40 → Heartbeat\n           └──────────────┴──────────────────┴───────────────┘\nHour 2:    2:10 → Fetch   │  2:25 → Process │  2:40 → Heartbeat\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Summary of All Active Cron Jobs\n\n**Existing jobs (unchanged):**\n- `github-push-sync` — Ever