{"type":"message","id":"ac7c2a4c","parentId":"9af511b8","timestamp":"2026-03-14T06:32:51.349Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is clarifying that they want the mimic dashboard content sized appropriately for a comfortable 5-minute reading experience. This likely means setting up pagination, word count limits, or auto-refresh functionality so users don't need more than 5 minutes to consume each daily brief.\n\nI'll set up a system where:\n1. Each daily brief is sized to be readable in ~5 minutes (roughly 3000-4000 words)\n2. Auto-refresh triggers every 5 minutes to fetch new content\n3. Content is paginated or truncated appropriately\n\nLet me create a script that handles this sizing and auto-refresh functionality."},{"type":"text","text":"I understand now! You want the **mimic dashboard content sized** so it takes about **5 minutes to read each daily brief**. This means implementing:\n\n1. **Word count limits** (~3000-4000 words per brief = typical 5-min reading)\n2. **Auto-refresh every 5 minutes** to fetch new content\n3. **Smart pagination** - break long transcripts into digestible chunks\n\n\nI'll build an auto-refresh system that handles content sizing, refresh cycles, and user-friendly navigation through daily briefs."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen3-5-9b","model":"qwen3.5-9b-claude-4.6-opus-reasoning-distilled","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773469879386}}
{"type":"message","id":"49852646","parentId":"ac7c2a4c","timestamp":"2026-03-14T06:34:04.828Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"openclaw-control-ui\",\n  \"id\": \"openclaw-control-ui\"\n}\n```\n\n[Sat 2026-03-14 09:34 GMT+3] Word count limits (~3000-4000 words per brief = typical 5-min reading) and that's it no auto refresh and no pagination"}],"timestamp":1773470044826}}
{"type":"message","id":"6f7e2002","parentId":"49852646","timestamp":"2026-03-14T06:38:49.415Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants a simple solution - just word count limiting for daily briefs, nothing complex like auto-refresh or pagination. I'll create a basic script that trims content to ~3000-4000 words per brief. This is straightforward: read the Telegram content, limit it to the target word count, and display it on the dashboard."},{"type":"text","text":"Got it! Simple solution - just **word count limiting** for daily briefs. No auto-refresh, no pagination. Just trim content to ~3500 words (~5 minutes reading time).\n\n\n## 📝 Creating Daily Brief Word-Limiter Script\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"277054142","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"D:\\AI_PROJECTS\\projects\\mimic\\daily_brief_limiter.py","content":"\"\"\"\nDaily Brief Word Limiter\nTrims Telegram content to ~3500 words (~5 min reading time)\n\"\"\"\nimport requests\nfrom bs4 import BeautifulSoup\n\ndef get_word_count(text):\n    \"\"\"Count words in text.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(text, str):\n        return 0\n    # Remove markdown and HTML\n    cleaned = re.sub(r'[\\[\\](?:.+:)?', '', text)\n    cleaned = re.sub(r'\\*+', '', cleaned)\n    cleaned = re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', ' ', cleaned)\n    words = len(cleaned.split())\n    return words\n\ndef trim_content(text, max_words=3500):\n    \"\"\"Trim content to max_words while preserving structure.\"\"\"\n    if not text or get_word_count(text) <= max_words:\n        return text\n    \n    # Split into sentences/chunks\n    chunks = re.split(r'(?<=[.!?])\\s+', text)\n    result = []\n    current_count = 0\n    \n    for chunk in chunks:\n        if not chunk.strip():\n            continue\n        chunk_words = get_word_count(chunk)\n        \n        if current_count + chunk_words <= max_words:\n            result.append(chunk)\n            current_count += chunk_words\n        else:\n            # Trim last chunk to fit\n            remaining_space = max_words - current_count\n            trimmed_chunk = trim_to_length(chunk, remaining_space)\n            if trimmed_chunk:\n                result.append(trimmed_chunk)\n            break\n    \n    return ' '.join(result)\n\ndef trim_to_length(text, target_chars):\n    \"\"\"Trim text to approximate character length.\"\"\"\n    if not text or len(text) <= target_chars:\n        return text\n    # Find a good break point (preferably at sentence boundary)\n    last_break = text.rfind('\\n')\n    period_pos = text.rfind('.', 0, target_chars)\n    exclamation = text.rfind('!', 0, target_chars)\n    question = text.rfind('?', 0, target_chars)\n    \n    break_points = [period_pos if period_pos >= 0 else -1,\n                    exclamation if exclamation >= 0 else -1,\n                    question if question >= 0 else -1]\n    break_points.append(last_break)  # Fall back to line break\n    \n    best_break = max(bp for bp in break_points if bp >= 0)\n    return text[:best_break + 1].strip()\n\ndef process_telegram_content(url, max_words=3500):\n    \"\"\"Fetch Telegram content and limit it.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        headers = {\n            'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36'\n        }\n        response = requests.get(url, headers=headers, timeout=10)\n        \n        if response.status_code == 200:\n            soup = BeautifulSoup(response.text, 'html.parser')\n            # Extract main content\n            text_elements = soup.find_all(['p', 'div', 'article'])\n            full_text = ''\n            for elem in text_elements:\n                full_text += elem.get_text() + '\\n'\n            \n            original_words = get_word_count(full_text)\n            trimmed_text = trim_content(full_text, max_words)\n            final_words = get_word_count(trimmed_text)\n            \n            print(f\"Original: {original_words} words → Trimmed: {final_words} words\")\n            return trimmed_text\n        else:\n            print(f\"Failed to fetch content: HTTP {response.status_code}\")\n            return \"\"\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error processing content: {e}\")\n        return \"\"\n","file_path":"D:\\AI_PROJECTS\\projects\\mimic\\daily_brief_limiter.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen3-5-9b","model":"qwen3.5-9b-claude-4.6-opus-reasoning-distilled","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773470044827}}
